# Normalise text files to LF in the working tree, not just in the
# repository.
#
# git's autocrlf otherwise checks out CRLF on Windows while storing LF, so
# every commit prints a "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warning and any tool
# that hashes or diffs file bytes sees something different locally than CI
# does. Keeping the working tree at LF removes a whole class of "it passes
# here and fails there" without costing anything on Windows, where every
# editor in use handles LF.
#
# This was added while chasing a lint result that differed between this
# machine and CI. Line endings turned out **not** to be the cause — the
# cause was `.gitignore` swallowing `src/data/` — but matching the
# repository in the working tree is worth doing on its own.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, never touched.
*.png binary
*.gif binary
*.mp4 binary
*.pdf binary
*.npz binary
*.pkl binary
*.safetensors binary
